e room reservations.","source_url":"https://www.uml.edu/myuml/submissions/2026/2026-01-23-13-06-22-welcome-back-from-uml-library.aspx","source_title":"Welcome Back from UML Library | UMass Lowell","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2026-01-28","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Library access and hours can vary by term; confirm current hours before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"tsongas-industrial-history-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Tsongas Industrial History Center","title":"Look for Hands-On History","subtitle":"115 John St., Lowell National Historical Park","notes":"If your weekend matches the second Saturday, drop in for the listed Hands-On History session and confirm the current activity on the center calendar.","short_summary":"A UMass Lowell–National Park Service partnership offering recurring hands-on history programming.","evidence_claim":"The Tsongas Industrial History Center lists free, no-registration Hands-On History drop-in events on the second Saturday of each month from 1 to 4 p.m.","source_url":"https://www.uml.edu/family/events.aspx","source_title":"Events and Programs | Family Programs | UMass Lowell","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"This activity is scheduled for the second Saturday of each month; confirm the date and program details before going.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lowell-national-historical-park-visitor-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Lowell National Historical Park Visitor Center","title":"Get oriented at the park visitor center","subtitle":"246 Market St., downtown Lowell","notes":"Pick up park information, ask a ranger about exhibits and tours, and use the stop to shape the rest of your downtown walk.","short_summary":"A downtown orientation point for Lowell National Historical Park sites and programs.","evidence_claim":"The Lowell National Historical Park Visitor Center at 246 Market Street provides information about park exhibits, guided tours, and special events.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/visitor-center.htm","source_title":"Visitor Center | Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2026-05-19","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The National Park Service lists daily seasonal hours; check the current operating-hours page before visiting.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mogan-cultural-center","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Patrick J. Mogan Cultural Center","title":"Explore the Mogan Cultural Center","subtitle":"40 French St., downtown Lowell","notes":"Walk through the two exhibits and give yourself time to compare the boarding-house recreation with the city’s wider cultural-history display.","short_summary":"A free cultural-history stop inside a historic Lowell boarding house.","evidence_claim":"The Mogan Cultural Center at 40 French Street contains the Into an 1840s Boarding House and One City, Many Cultures exhibits, with free admission.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/lowe/planyourvisit/placestogo.htm","source_title":"Places To Go | Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":"2026-01-24","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Observe posted hours; the National Park Service lists seasonal operating times for this location.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"northern-canal-walkway","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Northern Canal Walkway","title":"Finish with a daytime canal walk","subtitle":"Lowell National Historical Park canal district","notes":"Take a daylight walk along the canal, follow posted conditions, and leave bikes, skateboards, and roller skates off the walkway.","short_summary":"A pedestrian canal route connecting historic park areas.","evidence_claim":"Lowell National Historical Park identifies the Northern Canal Walkway as a pedestrian area and prohibits bicycles, skateboards, and roller skates there.","source_url":"https://www.nps.gov/lowe/learn/management/superintendent-s-compendium.htm","source_title":"Superintendent’s Compendium | Lowell National Historical Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use in daylight and follow posted closures; the route closes seasonally from School Street Bridge to Pawtucket Street Bridge.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
